{"name":"Sky Bus","hex":"#99c1d6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"bus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bokobaru."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A motor vehicle for transporting large numbers of people along roads.","A coach, a bus used for long travels."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skybus Airlines","blocks":[{"text":"Skybus Airlines Inc. was a privately held airline based in Columbus, Ohio, United States. It operated as an ultra low-cost carrier modeled after the European airline Ryanair, and aimed to be the least expensive airline in the United States. The business model was heavily reliant on flying routes where other airlines did not have direct flights, as Ryanair did in Europe, thus keeping competition to a minimum, and on flying into secondary airports, rather than heavily trafficked ones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/09/Skybus.svg/330px-Skybus.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skybus_Airlines"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky"},{"title":"Bus","blocks":[{"text":"A bus is a motor vehicle that carries significantly more passengers than an average car or van, but fewer than the average rail transport. It is most commonly used in public transport, but is also in use for charter purposes, or through private ownership. Although buses typically carry between 30 and 100 passengers, some buses have a capacity of up to 300 passengers. The most common type is the single-deck rigid bus, with double-decker and articulated buses carrying larger loads, and midibuses and minibuses carrying smaller loads. Coaches are used for longer-distance services. Many types of buses, such as city transit buses and inter-city coaches, charge a fare. Other types, such as elementary or secondary school buses or shuttle buses within a post-secondary education campus, are free. In many jurisdictions, bus drivers require a special large vehicle licence above and beyond a regular driving license."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/LTZ1328-19-20241030-160332.jpg/330px-LTZ1328-19-20241030-160332.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bus"},{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg/500px-Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg/1280px-Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg/500px-Skybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Skybus Airlines Airbus A319 at Port Columbus International Airport.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkybusplane_at_Port_Columbus_International_Airport.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Skybus_Airlines_billboard_along_Interstate_75_south_of_Dalton%2C_Georgia.jpg/500px-Skybus_Airlines_billboard_along_Interstate_75_south_of_Dalton%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Skybus_Airlines_billboard_along_Interstate_75_south_of_Dalton%2C_Georgia.jpg/500px-Skybus_Airlines_billboard_along_Interstate_75_south_of_Dalton%2C_Georgia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Billboard for service between Chattanooga and Columbus on I-75","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkybus_Airlines_billboard_along_Interstate_75_south_of_Dalton%2C_Georgia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Skybus_Wings.jpg/250px-Skybus_Wings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo